# The rail while a team works: the agent of the workspace, the agents it runs
# beside it, the shared task list, and one of their transcripts being read.
#
# This is the one scene that talks to the agent, because those rows only exist
# once it has started something. Both agents are asked to read and report,
# never to change a file.
title lmux team
size 140 38
pre lmux kill --all
pre rm -rf .devcontainer
run lmux team . --nested
wait 8
frame 1.6
type Start two agents in parallel: one describes internal/gateway in five lines, the other describes the README in five lines. Neither changes a file.
enter
wait 20
frame 2.4
film 3 1.4
# The rail is open by now, with a row per agent. Focusing it gives the keys
# below to the rail rather than to the agent.
keys M-[
wait 1.5
frame 2
# The shared task list of the team, and back to the rail.
keys t
wait 3
frame 2.6
keys q
wait 1.4
# The transcript of one of them: what it was asked, what it answered, and the
# tools it called. The rows are the lead section, the lead, the agents section
# and then the agents, so three moves land on the first of them.
keys Down
wait 0.5
keys Down
wait 0.5
keys Down
wait 0.8
keys r
wait 3.5
frame 2.6
keys q
wait 1.4
frame 2
